const DEADLINES=[{date:"Resolved",target:new Date("2026-06-22T00:00:00Z"),label:"Belarus Ultimatum — Elapsed",status:"Resolved",icon:"🇧🇾",color:"#22c55e",desc:"Window closed Jun 22 with partial compliance (relay shutdown). No further Ukrainian strikes on Belarusian territory followed — treated as a closed case pending any reversal."},{date:"Jul 7–8",target:new Date("2026-07-07T09:00:00Z"),label:"NATO Ankara Summit",status:"Concluded",icon:"🤝",color:"#5b8ec8",desc:"CONCLUDED, but the Patriot outcome didn't hold. Allies pledged $80B (~€70B) for Ukraine in 2026 and reaffirmed Article 5; Trump's apparent green light for Europe/Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles under license was walked back Jul 31 — he told a Cabinet meeting the US has 'not agreed' to license the technology, directly contradicting Zelensky's Jul 9 claim a deal was reached. Exposed starkly by the Aug 1 Kyiv attack (1 of 27 ballistic missiles intercepted). Russia's Turkish ceasefire push was rejected before the summit began."},{date:"Jul 24",target:new Date("2026-07-24T00:00:00Z"),label:"Ukraine Protest Deadline — Elapsed",status:"Elapsed",icon:"🇺🇦",color:"#dc2626",desc:"Deadline passed Jul 24 without resolution — BBC reports Zelensky is 'struggling to fix' the crisis. Fedorov still refuses any role but reinstatement; protests continue into a second week with no new defense minister named."},{date:"Expired",target:new Date("2026-08-16T00:00:00Z"),label:"Iran MoU Deadline — Expired",status:"Expired",icon:"☢️",color:"#ef4444",desc:"The 60-day Islamabad MoU window closed Aug 16 with both sides at an impasse — no framework, no extension, no announced consequence. Iran maintains it never considered the 60-day clock to have formally begun, so it never engaged in extension talks. Trump reiterated he'll soon declare Hormuz US territory; Iran's deputy FM countered the strait 'was Iran's, is Iran's, and will remain Iran's.' Enrichment, the missile programme and Hormuz governance all remain exactly where they were — this is a deadline that lapsed, not one that resolved."},{date:"Nov 10",target:new Date("2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"),label:"China Rare-Earth Truce Expires",status:"Upcoming",icon:"⛏️",color:"#eab308",desc:"The one major deadline still ahead rather than behind. After the Nov 2025 Xi-Trump meeting, MOFCOM suspended its October export-control rules for one year — to Nov 10, 2026 — with the US-specific bans suspended to Nov 27. Licensing requirements and the military end-use ban were never lifted, and analysts (Trivium) read the pause as calibration rather than retreat. If the suspension lapses without renewal, the 0.1% Chinese-origin rare-earth licensing rule bites on foreign products again, directly hitting the Western processing build-out tracked on this tab. On Sep 23, as Xi arrived for his Sep 24 White House summit, Treasury Secretary Bessent said the wider Busan trade truce had been extended two months to Jan 10, 2027, without saying which measures it covers; officials said rare-earth deliveries are still falling short, and the summit produced no rare-earth deal — so the MOFCOM Nov 10 date stands until Beijing formally extends it."}];
